<!-- ══════════════════════════════════════
     SECTION 3 — WHY 3M FOR PHILADELPHIA
     ══════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="m3-why">
  <div class="m3-why__container">

    <div class="m3-why__image-wrap">
      <img
        src="/images/3m-window-film-philadelphia-why.jpg"
        alt="Philadelphia red brick rowhome with large bay windows on a bright sunny summer day — the city’s heat and single-pane glass make the right window film critical"
        width="768"
        height="960"
        loading="lazy"
        class="m3-why__image"
      />
      <div class="m3-why__stat-card">
        <div class="m3-why__stat-item">
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12.75L11.25 15 15 9.75M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"/></svg>
          <span>IECC Climate Zone 4A &mdash; 4 full seasons</span>
        </div>
        <div class="m3-why__stat-divider"></div>
        <div class="m3-why__stat-item">
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12.75L11.25 15 15 9.75M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"/></svg>
          <span>~2,500 sunshine hours per year</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="m3-why__content">
      <span class="m3-why__eyebrow">Why 3M for Philadelphia</span>
      <h2 class="m3-why__headline">Philadelphia’s Climate Makes the Right Film Non-Negotiable</h2>
      <p class="m3-why__intro">
        Philadelphia sits in IECC Climate Zone 4A — a mixed-humid zone with genuine summers and genuine winters. That means a window film that only handles summer heat is only doing half the job. 3M is one of the few manufacturers with a product line engineered specifically for four-season performance: Sun Control for summer solar load, Thinsulate for winter insulation, and everything in between. Add Philadelphia’s large stock of aging single-pane rowhome glass and Center City high-rises with floor-to-ceiling glazing, and the range and precision of 3M’s lineup becomes a real advantage.
      </p>
      <ul class="m3-why__bullets">
        <li>
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M8 12l3 3 5-5" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
          Old rowhome single-pane glass loses heat fast in winter — 3M Thinsulate adds an insulating layer without replacing the window
        </li>
        <li>
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M8 12l3 3 5-5" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
          Center City offices with large glass walls face severe solar heat gain from south and west exposures — 3M Sun Control rejects up to 79%
        </li>
        <li>
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M8 12l3 3 5-5" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
          Retail and commercial properties on busy corridors benefit from 3M Scotchshield’s smash-and-grab deterrence
        </li>
        <li>
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M8 12l3 3 5-5" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
          All 3M architectural films are NFRC-certified — independently rated for VLT, SHGC, and U-value so you know exactly what you’re getting
        </li>
        <li>
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M8 12l3 3 5-5" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
          3M’s manufacturer warranty travels with the product — if a film fails within spec, 3M backs the replacement, not just the installer
        </li>
      </ul>
      <div class="m3-why__climate-facts">
        <div class="m3-why__climate-item">
          <span class="m3-why__climate-num">2,500</span>
          <span class="m3-why__climate-label">Sunshine hours per year</span>
        </div>
        <div class="m3-why__climate-item">
          <span class="m3-why__climate-num">87°F</span>
          <span class="m3-why__climate-label">Average July high</span>
        </div>
        <div class="m3-why__climate-item">
          <span class="m3-why__climate-num">Zone 4A</span>
          <span class="m3-why__climate-label">Mixed-humid, 4 seasons</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <a href="/contact/" class="m3-why__cta">
        Get a free film assessment &rarr;
        <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M4.5 12h15m0 0l-6.75-6.75M19.5 12l-6.75 6.75"/></svg>
      </a>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<!-- ══════════════════════════════════════
     SECTION 4 — RESIDENTIAL / COMMERCIAL SLIDER
     ══════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="m3-slider" id="m3Slider">
  <div class="m3-slider__track" id="m3Track">

    <!-- SLIDE 01: Residential -->
    <div class="m3-slider__slide" data-slide="0">
      <img src="/images/3m-window-film-philadelphia-residential.jpg" alt="Bright Philadelphia rowhouse living room with 3M window film on bay windows" class="m3-slider__bg" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="m3-slider__overlay"></div>
      <div class="m3-slider__content">
        <div class="m3-slider__step">01</div>
        <h2 class="m3-slider__title">Philadelphia homes<br/>deserve 3M precision</h2>
        <p class="m3-slider__desc">Philadelphia's housing stock runs on single-pane glass — beautiful to look through, terrible for heat retention in winter and solar gain in summer. 3M Thinsulate and Sun Control films are engineered specifically for this: one insulates, one rejects heat, and both protect without replacing your windows.</p>
        <div class="m3-slider__faq">
          <div class="m3-slider__faq-item">
            <button class="m3-slider__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Which 3M film is best for Philly rowhomes?<span class="m3-slider__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
            <div class="m3-slider__faq-a" hidden>It depends on your primary concern. For summer heat and glare, 3M Sun Control is the standard recommendation — it rejects up to 79% of solar heat. For year-round performance including winter insulation on older single-pane windows, 3M Thinsulate is often a better fit. We assess your glass and orientation during a free consultation before recommending.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="m3-slider__faq-item">
            <button class="m3-slider__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Will film change how my home looks from the street?<span class="m3-slider__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
            <div class="m3-slider__faq-a" hidden>Most residential 3M films are optically clear or very lightly tinted — virtually undetectable from street level. High-clarity spectrally selective options maintain a natural glass appearance while still rejecting significant heat. We'll show you samples before any installation.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="m3-slider__faq-item">
            <button class="m3-slider__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Can film go on my bay windows or historic glass?<span class="m3-slider__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
            <div class="m3-slider__faq-a" hidden>Yes — bay windows and older single-pane glass are among the most common residential applications we handle in Philadelphia. 3M makes specific film series approved for single-pane glass. We assess your glass type and condition before installation to ensure compatibility and long-term performance.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <a href="/contact/" class="m3-slider__cta">Get a residential estimate &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- SLIDE 02: Commercial -->
    <div class="m3-slider__slide" data-slide="1">
      <img src="/images/3m-window-film-philadelphia-commercial.jpg" alt="Modern Philadelphia Center City office with 3M Sun Control window film on floor-to-ceiling glass" class="m3-slider__bg" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="m3-slider__overlay"></div>
      <div class="m3-slider__content">
        <div class="m3-slider__step">02</div>
        <h2 class="m3-slider__title">Philadelphia businesses<br/>run on 3M performance</h2>
        <p class="m3-slider__desc">Center City high-rises, Old City storefronts, healthcare facilities, and University City campuses all share one problem: too much glass, too much solar heat, and HVAC systems working overtime. 3M Sun Control window film reduces cooling load by up to 30% — with payback periods averaging 2–4 years on commercial installations.</p>
        <div class="m3-slider__faq">
          <div class="m3-slider__faq-item">
            <button class="m3-slider__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">How quickly does 3M film pay back on commercial buildings?<span class="m3-slider__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
            <div class="m3-slider__faq-a" hidden>Most commercial installations with significant south- or west-facing glass see full payback within 2–4 years through HVAC savings alone. Larger glass footprints and high utility costs accelerate that timeline. 3M's energy consultants can provide a building-specific projection — ask us about it during your estimate.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="m3-slider__faq-item">
            <button class="m3-slider__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Will installation disrupt our operations?<span class="m3-slider__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
            <div class="m3-slider__faq-a" hidden>Minimal disruption. Our crews work floor by floor and can schedule evenings or weekends for occupied commercial spaces. We coordinate with building management on a project-by-project basis to minimize impact on tenants and daily operations.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="m3-slider__faq-item">
            <button class="m3-slider__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Does 3M film work on curtain wall and floor-to-ceiling glass?<span class="m3-slider__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
            <div class="m3-slider__faq-a" hidden>Yes — large commercial glass is where 3M film delivers its biggest results. Film is applied in panels with nearly invisible seams and performs consistently across curtain wall systems, storefront glass, and insulated glass units. We assess your glass type and building spec before recommending a product series.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <a href="/contact/" class="m3-slider__cta">Get a commercial estimate &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>

  <!-- Right nav -->
  <nav class="m3-slider__nav" aria-label="Slide navigation">
    <button class="m3-slider__nav-item m3-slider__nav-item--active" data-m3nav="0">
      <span class="m3-slider__nav-line"></span>
      <span class="m3-slider__nav-label">Residential</span>
    </button>
    <button class="m3-slider__nav-item" data-m3nav="1">
      <span class="m3-slider__nav-line"></span>
      <span class="m3-slider__nav-label">Commercial</span>
    </button>
  </nav>

  <!-- Arrows -->
  <button class="m3-slider__arrow m3-slider__arrow--prev" id="m3Prev" aria-label="Previous slide">
    <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="15 18 9 12 15 6"></polyline></svg>
  </button>
  <button class="m3-slider__arrow m3-slider__arrow--next" id="m3Next" aria-label="Next slide">
    <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"></polyline></svg>
  </button>

  <!-- Progress bar -->
