      <h2 class="m3-pl-row__heading">Scotchshield™ Safety &amp; Security Series — Glass retention when it matters most</h2>
      <p class="m3-pl-row__body">Glass is the weakest point in most buildings. When it breaks — from a smash-and-grab, a windstorm, spontaneous thermal stress, or forced entry — the shards are the hazard. 3M Scotchshield Safety &amp; Security Series films are applied to the interior glass surface where, on impact, they hold a broken pane together rather than letting it scatter. That single function changes the outcome of nearly every glass-failure event: it turns a shattered window into a cracked one, keeps occupants safe from flying fragments, and dramatically slows a forced-entry attempt. The series ranges from 4-mil films for standard safety glazing applications up to the heavy-duty 8-mil Ultra S800 for high-security facilities — all near-invisible at 87% or higher visible light transmission.</p>
      <p class="m3-pl-row__body">In Philadelphia, Scotchshield is most commonly installed on Old City and Center City retail storefronts (smash-and-grab deterrence), K–12 schools and university campuses (safety glazing upgrades without window replacement), and healthcare facilities with high public foot traffic. On commercial properties where blast or windstorm mitigation is a priority, the Scotchshield Ultra series can be paired with an Impact Protection Adhesive (IPA) sealant system for a fully bonded glass retention assembly. Important: Scotchshield holds glass together — it does not make glass unbreakable or guarantee protection from all injury or property damage.</p>

